@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Full GLM serving contract
+
+Apply after the recipe's model and compatibility patches. Runtime files are only cuda/server.py,
+cuda/reply_text.py, server/request_options.py, server/tools.py. Install jsonschema>=4.18.
+No numerical engine or family code changes. Use Mia's existing ThinkingOffTemplate: off
+closes the prompt's think block; do not replace it with PR159's low-effort mapping.
+
+Unknown explicit model ids, malformed schemas/choices/thinking controls, non-positive or
+non-integer reply budgets and out-of-range sampling values reject with HTTP400 before
+SSE. Omitted/null budgets retain defaults. Stops match answer text after separation,
+including tool arguments, not reasoning. Truncated tool openers/blocks are never answer
+content; length and disconnect may leave incomplete streamed JSON.
+
+GLM tool headers and argument deltas stream incrementally, including single-call policy.
+IDs/indexes remain stable; string values are escaped incrementally, typed values wait
+for a value closer. Only execute after a successful tool_calls finish, after JSON/schema
+validation. Do not execute on a closing brace alone. Mia's repair of missing arg_key is
+retained for nonstreamed parsing. If repair would disagree with emitted deltas, streaming
+fails and requires a nonstream retry. Do not silently rewrite previously emitted args.
+
+Baseline recipe tests predate max-effort and nullable-parameter support. The accompanying
+test diffs bring those expectations forward and update explicit changed API contracts.
+See the recipe validation report for CPU and live tests and client requirements.
